      "text": "The first differential run passes 18/29 and localizes the failures: Windows text-mode newlines, headers positional handling, slice’s write-before-validation order, and two legacy streaming-statistics tie/degradation behaviors. I’m fixing those root semantics now and probing frequency ties for stability before choosing an ordering rule; the important correction is that the official binary can emit a header before returning a range error, so parity includes partial output on failure, not just successful results."
